cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "dopt-augmentation: sequential D-optimal augmentation of an existing experimental record"
type: software
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-17
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22234202
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/skjang8/dopt-augmentation"
abstract: >-
  Sequential D-optimal selection that proposes the next experiments for a record
  whose conditions are known. It reads no measured response, so it runs on any
  process, and the whole set of additions can be fixed before the first of them
  is performed. Includes the process conditions and thickness measurements of
  the accompanying HfO2 PEALD study.
keywords:
  - design of experiments
  - D-optimal design
  - one-factor-at-a-time
  - atomic layer deposition
  - plasma-enhanced atomic layer deposition
  - hafnium oxide
  - machine learning
  - thin film thickness
